# Plugin Distribution Server API

## Overview

This API provides integration with plugin distribution servers, allowing end users to add their own custom servers for hosting plugins.

## Architecture

- **IPluginServerService**: Manages registered plugin servers (CRUD operations)
- **IPluginPackageService**: Queries and downloads packages from servers
- **PluginServerOptions**: Configuration for default servers and HTTP settings

## Key Endpoints (per Packages Consumer API Reference)

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `GET /api/applications/{applicationId}/packages` | List all packages (filter by os, arch) |
| `GET /api/applications/{applicationId}/packages/{packageId}` | Get package details |
| `GET /api/applications/{applicationId}/packages/{packageId}/download` | Download ZIP (optional version param) |
| `GET /api/applications/{applicationId}/packages/{packageId}/icon` | Get package icon |

## Usage

```csharp
// Register services
services.AddPluginServerServices(options =>
{
    options.DefaultServers = new[]
    {
        new DefaultServer
        {
            Id = "official",
            Name = "Official Plugins",
            BaseUrl = "https://plugins.example.com/",
            ApplicationId = "my-app"
        }
    };
});

// Add a custom server
var server = new PluginServer
{
    Id = "custom",
    Name = "My Plugins",
    BaseUrl = new Uri("https://my-plugins.example.com/"),
    ApplicationId = "my-app"
};
await pluginServerService.AddServerAsync(server);

// Search packages across all enabled servers
var results = await pluginPackageService.SearchPackagesAsync("my-app");

// Download a package
var download = await pluginPackageService.DownloadPackageAsync(
    server, "my-app", "my-plugin");
```

## Supported Filters

- **OS**: "win", "mac", "linux", "android"
- **Architecture**: "x64", "arm64", "x86", "armv7"

## Content Verification

Downloads include SHA-256 hash verification (format: "sha256:...").
